https://github.com/tessera-io/platform/pull/402

The date filter now resolves ranges in the plant's timezone instead of the browser's. "Last 7 days" for a plant in Ohio means Ohio days, which is what every customer assumed it already did. Presets and custom ranges persist per plant.

Big diff, sorry. Read it in this order: filters/range.py, then the API change, then the React bits.

Known subtlety: the persisted range is stored as UTC and restored in local, which is fine as long as restore goes through the same resolver. There's a test for the preset case.

